1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,900
 The mix on the borrow side has been it shifted more towards primes.

2
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:08,700
 They provide margin to their clients and then they do a significant amounts of OTC trading,

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,500
 but also on-chain hedge funds and yield funds.

4
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:17,700
 So they might want to borrow from us against collateral that is actually forming part of a yield strategy they're doing on-chain,

5
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:20,200
 but they borrow from us to lever those strategies.

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,900
 And then the other one would be liquid token funds.

7
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:24,500
 So they might have a position they have high conviction in.

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:29,700
 It's too expensive for them to finance a position using perps and they don't want to risk a liquidation.

9
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:32,600
 So instead what they do is they could purchase the position,

10
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:38,200
 post it to us as collateral, borrow dollars and lever up that position or invest in other deals that they want to.

11
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:42,900
 Increasingly what shifted this year is we've started taking in more family offices and high net worths.

12
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,300
 You know, they might want to purchase real estate using crypto holdings that they've accumulated over a number of years.

13
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,900
 From us, what they're looking for is certainty on rates,

14
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:54,300
 making sure that they almost never are in danger of getting liquidated.

15
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:58,800
 So they'll post significant over collateralization and then counterparty risk.

